L"], "excluded_candidates": ["Localized infection: low-tier due to normal physical exam and systemic leukocytosis", "Chronic myeloproliferative neoplasm: normal differential and absence of splenomegaly reduce likelihood", "Hyperparathyroidism: hypercalcemia possible but lacks parathyroid-specific evidence", "Leukemia/lymphoma: possible but requires bone marrow involvement evidence not yet present", "Paraneoplastic syndrome: abdominal pain and hypercalcemia suggest this, but imaging/cancer history missing"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (fever, weight loss, fatigue)", "Marked leukocytosis with unspecified cause", "Hypercalcemia of uncertain origin", "Elevated leukocyte alkaline phosphatase (suggestive of chronic myeloid rather than lymphoid processes)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.41686469823113836, "posterior": 0.41686469823113836, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.16491350699253826, "posterior": 0.16491350699253826, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.13865012333094415, "posterior": 0.13865012333094415, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.07299528111142713, "posterior": 0.07299528111142713, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.17865629924191648, "posterior": 0.17865629924191648, "danger": 0.4, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.2, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.2, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B2", "B3", "B4", "B5"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the hypercalcemia (Ca2+ 10.9 mEq/L) support a plasma cell disorder like multiple myeloma as a lymphoproliferative alternative?", "summary": "Hypercalcemia weakly supports plasma cell disorders but is insufficient alone due to the absence of other defining features like anemia or monoclonal protein."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the recent cold and normal differential support a reactive leukemoid reaction as a benign cause of leukocytosis?", "summary": "The cold history and normal differential weakly support reactive causes, but lack of infection markers reduces this likelihood."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the elevated leukocyte alkaline phosphatase (LAP) level argue against chronic myeloid leukemia (CML) as a subset of chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms?", "summary": "Elevated LAP strongly argues against CML, which typically shows decreased LAP, but this does not favor other branches."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the normal leukocyte differential (no blasts) argue against lymphoid neoplasm with increased blasts in favor of non-malignant causes?", "summary": "Absence of blasts weakly argues against lymphoid neoplasms with increased blasts, shifting probability toward non-malignant causes."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the normal leukocyte differential argue against multiple myeloma (plasma cell disorder) despite hypercalcemia?", "summary": "Normal differential weakly argues against multiple myeloma, which typically presents with abnormal differential or blasts."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of infection markers (e.g., CRP, neutrophil left shift) despite constitutional symptoms argue against a leukemoid reaction?", "summary": "Lack of infection markers weakly argues against leukemoid reaction, which is typically associated with infection/inflammation."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B3", 0.399], ["B1", 0.388], ["B2", 0.213]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.265], ["B3", 0.229], ["B5", 0.227]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "No branch meets posterior >= 0.75 for confirmation. B2.3 (Multiple Myeloma) remains a dangerous unresolved alternative with posterior 0.064. Tree depth (2) is below max (3). Further discriminators like peripheral blood smear, bone marrow biopsy, or monoclonal protein testing are needed to refine the differential."}, "turn_budget_used": 2, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.65, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.26477064902876085, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic lymphoma"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic myeloid leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Leukemoid reaction"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'CSF Leukocytosis', 'Leukocytosis', 'Infection associated neutropenia'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B3", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.399}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B1", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "posterior": 0.417, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 1}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 0, "disconfirming": 0, "last_disconfirming_digest": ""}, "action_intents": [{"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B5", "B2", "B3"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=60%, source=primekg]\n\nChronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm vs Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n\nChronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm vs Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts:\n  Favours first:  abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n  Favours second: abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, elevated serum creatinine\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n\nRelated to Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm: bone marrow cancer, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, not otherwise specified\n\nRelated to Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, lymphoid leukemia (disease), lymphoma\n\nRelated to Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: cd4+/cd56+ hematodermic neoplasm, hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, mast cell neoplasm\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 59-year-old man presents to his primary care physician for fatigue → fatigue → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  A 59-year-old man presents to his primary care physician for fatigue → fatigue → Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts"}
